WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:04.214
- Oh, I probably have as big
an ego as anybody, you know.

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.756
(cheerful music)

00:00:07.756 --> 00:00:09.874
- [Voiceover] Well hey
there, look, it's Willie.

00:00:09.874 --> 00:00:12.693
- [Voiceover] 30 years ago, a
chess match with Ray Charles

00:00:12.693 --> 00:00:16.984
taught a very confident
Willie a lesson in humility.

00:00:16.984 --> 00:00:18.676
- Ray and I were doing a show in Austin,

00:00:18.676 --> 00:00:21.290
he was staying over at the hotel,

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.055
and I went over to say
hello, he comes to the door,

00:00:24.055 --> 00:00:27.984
we walked in, there was a little
light in the hallway there,

00:00:27.984 --> 00:00:32.002
then we walked into the living
room, there was no light.

00:00:32.002 --> 00:00:35.313
And he sat down here and I sat down there,

00:00:35.313 --> 00:00:38.086
he got out the chess board.

00:00:38.086 --> 00:00:42.153
And his chess pieces were
all, there were no color,

00:00:42.153 --> 00:00:45.767
they were all the same color,
unpainted wood, you know?

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:49.772
But he could feel of 'em
and tell what they were.

00:00:49.772 --> 00:00:50.605
- [Voiceover] Hey, hey, hey.

00:00:50.605 --> 00:00:53.515
- So needless to say, he
kicked my ass about three games

00:00:53.515 --> 00:00:56.908
in a row and I said thank
you, Ray, let's go sing.

00:00:56.908 --> 00:00:59.888
♫ Whoa, I believe they were prayin’

00:00:59.888 --> 00:01:01.500
♫ Prayin’ for the lovers

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.991
♫ Yeah they was ♫

00:01:02.991 --> 00:01:05.138
- But I didn't tell him that
the next time we played,

00:01:05.138 --> 00:01:08.544
I wanted to do it with
the lights on (laughs).

00:01:08.544 --> 00:01:11.627
(mellow piano music)

